/* ===== sim/elements.js: the curated element library: LINE_WEIGHTS, COLOURS, STYLES, ELEMENTS (PR 1) =====
   Everything a design is built from. The player never draws freehand and Ink never renders free text as art: every motif,
   word, frame, fill and texture is one entry here. Shapes are in docs/SIM-CONTRACT.md (section sim/elements.js).
     LINE_WEIGHTS   liner groupings (1RL fine line ... 14RL bold); design.js maps them to millimetres (LINE_MM)
     COLOURS        the 13 ink colours: name, hex, light (perceived lightness 0..1, L* / 100), read by SKIN_CONTRAST
     STYLES         the 9 styles: ageFactor (how well it holds), lineRange, palette, blendsWith (symmetric), demandCurve
                    (piecewise linear [year, mult] 2000..2030, read by market.js), clientSegments
     ELEMENTS       ~130 elements. path = SVG path data in a 0..100 box, drawn to be STROKED as linework (round caps and
                    joins; stipple and dot textures are tiny segments that a round cap turns into dots). fill = optional path
                    for solid or shaded areas (nonzero fill rule): how dark it goes is the design element's own fill 0..1.
                    Since 0.1.19.0 the traditional motifs fill their whole region (petals, wings, blade, body), so a
                    coloured piece comes out packed; fineline motifs, lettering, frames and textures stay line-only.
                    A fill keeps inside the path's own box (old layouts keep their sizes); overlapping parts run the
                    same way round, and a hole (a highlight, an eyespot, a ring) runs the other way (rev(), symF()).
                    fill2 / colour2 (0.1.25.0) = an optional second part (leaves, stems) in a fixed colour (PART2), the
                    same rules as fill (closed, inside the box, same way round); SIM.fill2Colour(def, colour, style) gives
                    its ink: the element's own on a black and grey piece, black where the style has no such colour.
                    src = "original" (drawn by Claude Code for Ink / Longlight Interactive) or a key into art/CREDITS.md.
                    unlock = "start" | "style:<style id>:<skill level 1..10>" | "rnd:<research id>".
     SIM.elementById(id) -> element or null (a Map built once).
   Geometric, botanical and pattern art is generated below by small helpers (seeded, no Math.random), so the shipped file
   stays small; the result is still plain path strings. Check and preview: node tools/element-sheet.js --png sheet.png */
